The Coast Guard will enforce the regulations in 33 CFR 100.1105 establishing regulated areas in the navigable waters of San Francisco Bay for the annual U.S. Navy and City of San Francisco sponsored Fleet Week Parade of Ships and Blue Angels demonstrations from October 8 through October 11, 2026. Fleet Week Air Show Box buoys will be in position from October 7 through October 12, 2026, at the following locations: 

center point, 37.81680, -122.42650;
southwest corner, 37.81020, -122.44643; 
northwest corner, 37.81855, -122.44780; 
northeast corner, 37.82315, -122.40590; 
and southeast corner, 37.81480, -122.40453. 

Mariners are advised to use caution when transiting in the vicinity of the buoyed air show box. All mariners are advised to transit the area with caution.

The Scripps Institution of Oceanography research vessel ROGER REVELLE (Call Sign KAOU) will conduct surface to floor oceanographic operations from October 8 to November 5, 2026, in the vicinity of the following waypoints: 

36.958736, -122.599167; 
36.958736, -121.077666; 
35.439742, -121.077666; and 
35.439742, -122.599167. 

The exact timing and location of each station will depend on operational concerns and weather conditions. During over-the-side operations, the vessel will be restricted in its ability to maneuver; all traffic is requested to give ROGER REVELLE a wide berth. The R/V ROGER REVELLE will monitor VHF-FM channels 16 and 13. Mariners are advised to use caution when transiting the area. For further comments or details, contact Heather Galiher at 858-226-8761. All mariners are advised to transit the area with caution.
